/-!
# Coherence of the symmetric powers of a sheaf of modules

Let `(X, 𝒪_X)` be a ringed space and `F` a coherent sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules. Then `Symⁿ F` is
coherent for every `n > 0`. This is the symmetric third of clause (4) of Stacks Tag 01CK; the
tensor third is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_tensorPower` in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorPowerCoherent`.

The proof uses the exact sequence

`⊕_{p < n - 1} Tⁿ(F) ⟶ Tⁿ(F) ⟶ Symⁿ(F) ⟶ 0`,

whose first map is the family of **slot-wise relators** `𝟙 - τ_p` of
`StacksFrontier.LinearAlgebra.TensorAlgebra.SymmetricQuotient`: over a commutative ring the kernel
of `Tⁿ(M) ⟶ Symⁿ(M)` is the sum of the ranges of the `n - 1` endomorphisms transposing two
adjacent slots. Since that algebraic identity quantifies over no generating family of `M`, the
sequence of *sectionwise* powers of a presheaf of modules is exact over every object of the site,
so sheafifying it — sheafification of presheaves of modules is a left adjoint and so preserves
cokernels and coproducts — presents `Symⁿ F` as the cokernel of a map between coherent sheaves.

Compared with the sequence `⊕_J T^{n-2}(F) ⟶ Tⁿ(F) ⟶ Symⁿ(F) ⟶ 0` of the Stacks Project, this
sequence has two advantages. Its first term is coherent for every `n > 0` by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_tensorPower`, so closure of coherence under cokernels finishes
the clause with no appeal to Tag 01BY and no degree-zero case; and the exactness needs no
localization to an open over which `F` is generated by finitely many sections, and hence no
stalkwise argument.

## Main definitions

* `PresheafOfModules.symQuotHom`: the sectionwise quotient `Tⁿ ⟶ Symⁿ` of presheaves of modules.
* `PresheafOfModules.slotRelHom`: the sectionwise slot-wise relator endomorphism of `Tⁿ`.
* `PresheafOfModules.relHom`: the first map of the sequence, out of the coproduct of the `n - 1`
  copies of `Tⁿ`.
* `PresheafOfModules.symQuotShortComplex`: the three-term complex of presheaves of modules.
* `SheafOfModules.symmetricPowerCokernelIso`: **`Symⁿ F` is the cokernel of the sheafified
  relator map.**

## Main results

* `SymmetricAlgebra.algHom_mapₛₗ` and `SymPow.symMapₛₗ_symQuot`: base change commutes with the
  canonical map from the tensor algebra to the symmetric algebra, and with its degree-`n` part.
  These are the naturality statements that make the sectionwise maps morphisms of presheaves.
* `PresheafOfModules.symQuotShortComplex_exact` and `PresheafOfModules.epi_symQuotHom`: the
  complex is exact at the middle term and its second map is an epimorphism, hence
  `PresheafOfModules.symQuotIsCokernel`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_symmetricPower`: **clause (4) of Tag 01CK for the symmetric
  powers** — each symmetric power of positive degree of a coherent sheaf of modules on a ringed
  space is coherent.

## Implementation notes

**Why the coproduct is the categorical one.** Objectwise exactness is read off from
`TensorAlgebra.exists_sum_slotRelMap`, which produces an explicit `Fin (n - 1)`-indexed family
whose sum is the given element of the kernel; the preimage in the coproduct is the corresponding
sum of the images of the coproduct injections. So no description of the sections of a coproduct
of presheaves of modules is needed, and in particular the injections are never claimed to be
jointly surjective on sections.

**Where the two sheafified objects are identified.** The degree-`n` piece of the tensor algebra
and the degree-`n` symmetric power of a sheaf of modules are the sheafifications of the
sectionwise powers of its underlying presheaf, by `SheafOfModules.tensorPieceSheafifyIso` and
`SheafOfModules.symmetricPowerSheafifyIso`, for an arbitrary package of algebras. Those two
isomorphisms are the only point of contact between this file and the construction of the three
algebras.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CK)
* [Stacks Project, Section 17.21](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite

universe v u w

/-! ### Base change and the canonical map to the symmetric algebra -/

namespace SymmetricAlgebra

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
  {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N]

/-- **Base change commutes with the canonical map from the tensor algebra to the symmetric
algebra.** -/
theorem algHom_mapₛₗ (φ : R →+* S) (u : M →ₛₗ[φ] N) (x : TensorAlgebra R M) :
    SymmetricAlgebra.algHom S N (TensorAlgebra.mapₛₗ φ u x) =
      SymmetricAlgebra.mapₛₗ φ u (SymmetricAlgebra.algHom R M x) := by
  induction x using TensorAlgebra.induction with
  | algebraMap r =>
      rw [TensorAlgebra.mapₛₗ_algebraMap, AlgHom.commutes, AlgHom.commutes,
        SymmetricAlgebra.mapₛₗ_algebraMap]
  | ι m =>
      have h1 : SymmetricAlgebra.algHom R M (TensorAlgebra.ι R m) =
        SymmetricAlgebra.ι R M m := rfl
      have h2 : SymmetricAlgebra.algHom S N (TensorAlgebra.ι S (u m)) =
        SymmetricAlgebra.ι S N (u m) := rfl
      rw [TensorAlgebra.mapₛₗ_ι, h2, h1, SymmetricAlgebra.mapₛₗ_ι]
  | mul a b ha hb => simp only [map_mul]; rw [ha, hb]
  | add a b ha hb => simp only [map_add]; rw [ha, hb]

end SymmetricAlgebra

namespace SymPow

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
  {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N]

/-- **The degree-`k` part of the canonical map to the symmetric algebra commutes with base
change.** -/
theorem symMapₛₗ_symQuot (k : ℕ) (φ : R →+* S) (u : M →ₛₗ[φ] N)
    (t : TensorAlgebra.gradedPiece R k M) :
    symMapₛₗ k φ u (TensorAlgebra.symQuot k t) =
      TensorAlgebra.symQuot k (TensorAlgebra.powMapₛₗ k φ u t) :=
  Subtype.ext (by
    rw [symMapₛₗ_coe, TensorAlgebra.coe_symQuot, TensorAlgebra.coe_symQuot,
      TensorAlgebra.powMapₛₗ_coe, SymmetricAlgebra.algHom_mapₛₗ])

end SymPow

/-! ### The sectionwise sequence of presheaves of modules -/

namespace PresheafOfModules

section Sectionwise

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {O : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}}
  (F : PresheafOfModules.{w} (O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat))

/-- `TensorAlgebra.symQuot` with its type spelled at the sections of `tensorPow` and `symPow`.
The two types are definitionally equal; the retyping is a separate declaration for the reason
documented in `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorAlgebraBundle`. -/
def symQuotApp (k : ℕ) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (tensorPow k F).obj X →ₗ[(O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat).obj X] (symPow k F).obj X :=
  TensorAlgebra.symQuot k

/-- **The sectionwise quotient `Tᵏ ⟶ Symᵏ`**, as a morphism of presheaves of modules. -/
def symQuotHom (k : ℕ) : tensorPow k F ⟶ symPow k F where
  app X := ModuleCat.ofHom (symQuotApp F k X)
  naturality {_ _} f := ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun t =>
    (SymPow.symMapₛₗ_symQuot k ((O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat).map f).hom (F.restrictₛₗ f) t).symm)

/-- `TensorAlgebra.slotRelMap` with its type spelled at the sections of `tensorPow`. -/
def slotRelApp (k : ℕ) (p : Fin (k - 1)) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (tensorPow k F).obj X →ₗ[(O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat).obj X] (tensorPow k F).obj X :=
  TensorAlgebra.slotRelMap k p

/-- **The sectionwise slot-wise relator endomorphism of `Tᵏ`**, as a morphism of presheaves of
modules. -/
def slotRelHom (k : ℕ) (p : Fin (k - 1)) : tensorPow k F ⟶ tensorPow k F where
  app X := ModuleCat.ofHom (slotRelApp F k p X)
  naturality {_ _} f := ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun t =>
    TensorAlgebra.slotRelMap_powMapₛₗ k p ((O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat).map f).hom
      (F.restrictₛₗ f) t)

/-- The sectionwise quotient acts on sections as `TensorAlgebra.symQuot`. -/
@[simp]
theorem symQuotHom_app_apply (k : ℕ) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (t : (tensorPow k F).obj X) :
    Hom.app (symQuotHom F k) X t = TensorAlgebra.symQuot k t := rfl

/-- The sectionwise relator acts on sections as `TensorAlgebra.slotRelMap`. -/
@[simp]
theorem slotRelHom_app_apply (k : ℕ) (p : Fin (k - 1)) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (t : (tensorPow k F).obj X) :
    Hom.app (slotRelHom F k p) X t = TensorAlgebra.slotRelMap k p t := rfl

/-- The source of the relator sequence: one copy of `Tᵏ` for each of the `k - 1` adjacent slot
pairs. -/
abbrev relSource (k : ℕ) : PresheafOfModules.{w} (O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) :=
  ∐ fun _ : Fin (k - 1) => tensorPow k F

/-- **The first map of the relator sequence.** -/
def relHom (k : ℕ) : relSource F k ⟶ tensorPow k F :=
  Sigma.desc fun p => slotRelHom F k p

/-- On the `p`-th summand of the source, the relator map is the `p`-th slot-wise relator. -/
theorem relHom_app_ι (k : ℕ) (p : Fin (k - 1)) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (t : (tensorPow k F).obj X) :
    Hom.app (relHom F k) X
        (Hom.app (Sigma.ι (fun _ : Fin (k - 1) => tensorPow k F) p) X t) =
      TensorAlgebra.slotRelMap k p t :=
  congrArg (fun φ : tensorPow k F ⟶ tensorPow k F => Hom.app φ X t)
    (Sigma.ι_comp_desc (fun p => slotRelHom F k p) p)

/-- The relator map followed by the quotient `Tᵏ ⟶ Symᵏ` is zero. -/
theorem relHom_comp_symQuotHom (k : ℕ) : relHom F k ≫ symQuotHom F k = 0 :=
  Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun p => by
    rw [relHom, Sigma.ι_comp_desc_assoc, comp_zero]
    exact hom_ext fun X => ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun t =>
      TensorAlgebra.symQuot_relMap _ t)

/-- **The three-term complex of presheaves of modules** `⊕ Tᵏ ⟶ Tᵏ ⟶ Symᵏ`. -/
def symQuotShortComplex (k : ℕ) :
    ShortComplex (PresheafOfModules.{w} (O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat)) :=
  ShortComplex.mk (relHom F k) (symQuotHom F k) (relHom_comp_symQuotHom F k)

/-- **The complex is exact at the middle term**, because over every object the kernel of
`Tᵏ ⟶ Symᵏ` is the sum of the ranges of the `k - 1` slot-wise relator maps
(`TensorAlgebra.exists_sum_slotRelMap`). -/
theorem symQuotShortComplex_exact (k : ℕ) : (symQuotShortComplex F k).Exact := by
  refine exact_of_sectionwise _ fun X t => ⟨fun ht => ?_, fun ht => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := TensorAlgebra.exists_sum_slotRelMap t ht
    have hmem : t ∈ LinearMap.range (ModuleCat.Hom.hom (Hom.app (relHom F k) X)) := by
      rw [hc]
      exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun p _ => ⟨_, relHom_app_ι F k p X (c p)⟩
    exact hmem
  · obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := ht
    exact congrArg (fun φ : relSource F k ⟶ symPow k F => Hom.app φ X s)
      (relHom_comp_symQuotHom F k)

/-- The sectionwise quotient `Tᵏ ⟶ Symᵏ` is an epimorphism, since it is surjective on sections. -/
instance epi_symQuotHom (k : ℕ) : Epi (symQuotHom F k) :=
  epi_of_surjective fun _ => TensorAlgebra.surjective_symQuot k

/-- **`Tᵏ ⟶ Symᵏ` is a cokernel of the relator map.** -/
def symQuotIsCokernel (k : ℕ) :
    IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ (symQuotHom F k) (relHom_comp_symQuotHom F k)) :=
  haveI : Epi (symQuotShortComplex F k).g := epi_symQuotHom F k
  (symQuotShortComplex_exact F k).gIsCokernel

/-- The categorical cokernel of the relator map is the presheaf of sectionwise symmetric
powers. -/
def cokernelRelHomIso (k : ℕ) : cokernel (relHom F k) ≅ symPow k F :=
  IsColimit.coconePointUniqueUpToIso (cokernelIsCokernel (relHom F k)) (symQuotIsCokernel F k)

end Sectionwise

end PresheafOfModules

/-! ### Sheafifying the sequence -/

namespace SheafOfModules

section Sheafify

open PresheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  {Osharp : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  (G : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Osharp))

/-- Sheafification of presheaves of modules along the identity of the structure sheaf is a left
adjoint, hence preserves cokernels and coproducts. -/
instance isLeftAdjoint_sheafification :
    (PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification J (𝟙 Osharp.obj)).IsLeftAdjoint :=
  ⟨_, ⟨PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (toRingCatMap J (𝟙 Osharp.obj))⟩⟩

/-- **The degree-`n` symmetric power of a sheaf of modules is the cokernel of the sheafified
slot-wise relator map.** -/
def symmetricPowerCokernelIso (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras J G) (n : ℕ) :
    A.symmetricPower n ≅
      cokernel ((PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification J (𝟙 Osharp.obj)).map
        (relHom (valPresheaf J G) n)) :=
  symmetricPowerSheafifyIso J A n ≪≫
    ((PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification J (𝟙 Osharp.obj)).mapIso
      (cokernelRelHomIso (valPresheaf J G) n)).symm ≪≫
    PreservesCokernel.iso _ _

set_option maxHeartbeats 1600000 in
-- elaborating `PreservesCoproduct.iso` for the module sheafification of the relator source is heavy
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000 in
/-- The sheafification of the source of the relator sequence is the coproduct of `n - 1` copies
of the sheafified degree-`n` tensor power. -/
def sheafifyRelSourceIso (n : ℕ) :
    (PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification J (𝟙 Osharp.obj)).obj
        (relSource (valPresheaf J G) n) ≅
      ∐ fun _ : Fin (n - 1) =>
        (PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification J (𝟙 Osharp.obj)).obj
          (tensorPow n (valPresheaf J G)) :=
  PreservesCoproduct.iso (PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification J (𝟙 Osharp.obj))
    (fun _ : Fin (n - 1) => tensorPow n (valPresheaf J G))

end Sheafify

end SheafOfModules

/-! ### Coherence -/

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace _root_.Stacks.PresheafOfModules

variable {X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u}}
  (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))

/-- **Each symmetric power of positive degree of a coherent sheaf of modules on a ringed space is
coherent.** This is clause (4) of [Stacks, Tag 01CK] for the symmetric powers. The sequence used
is `⊕_{p < n - 1} Tⁿ(F) ⟶ Tⁿ(F) ⟶ Symⁿ(F) ⟶ 0`, whose first term is coherent by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_tensorPower` and `isCoherent_sigma`, so that closure of
coherence under cokernels finishes. -/
@[stacks 01CK "symmetric powers of a coherent module, in positive degree"]
theorem isCoherent_symmetricPower [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent F]
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) F) (n : ℕ) (hn : 0 < n) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent (A.symmetricPower n) := by
  have hT : IsCoherent ((PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (𝟙 X.sheaf.obj)).obj
      (PresheafOfModules.tensorPow n
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.valPresheaf (Osharp := X.sheaf)
          (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) F))) :=
    (coherentModules _).prop_of_iso
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.tensorPieceSheafifyIso (Osharp := X.sheaf)
        (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) A n)
      ((TensorOver.isCoherent_iff _).1 (isCoherent_tensorPower F A n hn))
  have hSrc : IsCoherent ((PresheafOfModules.moduleSheafification
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (𝟙 X.sheaf.obj)).obj
      (PresheafOfModules.relSource
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.valPresheaf (Osharp := X.sheaf)
          (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) F) n)) :=
    (coherentModules _).prop_of_iso
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.sheafifyRelSourceIso (Osharp := X.sheaf)
        (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) F n).symm
      (isCoherent_sigma _ fun _ => hT)
  exact (TensorOver.isCoherent_iff _).2
    ((coherentModules _).prop_of_iso
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.symmetricPowerCokernelIso (Osharp := X.sheaf)
        (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) F A n).symm
      ((coherentModules _).prop_cokernel _ hSrc hT))

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
